  "question": {
    "math_academy_id": "q-181805",
    "knowledge_point_id": "d9f0da82-f79b-5056-ac99-b401eb1630c7",
    "knowledge_point": "Describing Rectangular Sets Using Set-Builder Notation",
    "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14096165/assets/40f8e6728cd7108f5026bd87debfbf60b616965686065c8e60f0d3ab741e52e4.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,{{field-2}}\\le x\\le {{field-3}},\\,{{field-4}}\\le y\\le {{field-5}}}\n$$",
    "worked_solution": "A point $P(x,y)$ lies inside or on the rectangle's edges if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1\\le x\\le 6,\\,3\\le y\\le 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMoreover, since *every* real value in these intervals is included, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 6,\\,3\\le y\\le 5}\n$$",
